'''Eden''' is a [[character]] unlocked by completing {{s|Womb}} for the first time. Uniquely, they are only playable by spending '''Eden Tokens''', which are awarded every time {{E|Mom's Heart}}, {{E|It Lives!}}, {{E|Ultra Greed}}, or {{E|The Beast}} is defeated.

Each time a game is started as Eden, one token is spent and a new Eden is randomly generated based on the seed: They will have a random hairstyle, base stats, active [[item]], passive item, and either a [[trinket]], [[pill]], or [[card|card/rune]].

Eden's stats are centered around Isaac's and are randomized within a set range. They will spawn with a combination of [[Red Heart container]]s and {{E|Soul Heart}}s.

''For details regarding the exact generation of an Eden Run, see [[Eden Generation]].''

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|na+}} Holding R to reset doesn't work with Eden, and every time you start a new run, you use up one Eden token.
** After starting a run and transforming into another character (using items like {{i|Ankh}} or {{i|Clicker}}), holding R to reset will work and start a new run as Eden, even if you don't have tokens.
* {{dlc|a+}} Holding R to reset will consume an Eden Token and start a new run.
* {{dlc|nr}} Eden can start with most items, including {{i|The Negative}} or {{i|The Polaroid}} if unlocked.
** {{i|Key Piece 1}}, {{i|Key Piece 2}}, {{i|Broken Shovel 1}}, {{i|Broken Shovel 2}} and {{i|Mom's Shovel}} cannot be granted.
* {{dlc+|r}} A [[Item Tags noeden|noeden item tag]] determines which items Eden cannot start with. These include {{i|Knife Piece 1}}, {{i|Knife Piece 2}}, {{i|Dogma}}, {{i|Dad's Note}}, {{i|Recall}} and {{i|Hold}}.{{dlc-}}
** {{i|Broken Glass Cannon|r+}} cannot be granted.
* {{dlc|a+}} Eden Tokens are not awarded for killing Mom's Heart or It Lives in {{s|The Void|n}}.
* It is possible to achieve an ending as Eden while not getting another token if the player defeats Mom and earns a Void Portal, then defeats Delirium. This will count as a victory, but no Eden Token will be earned. This can also be achieved by using Sacrifice Rooms to teleport to the Dark Room.

== Item Interactions ==
* {{i|Birthright}}: Spawns 3 random items from random item pools. Only one can be taken.
* {{i|Genesis}}: If Eden uses Genesis it will reroll the character as if it was a new run (new starting items, new hairstyle and new stats).
* {{i|Glowing Hourglass}}: {{dlcalt|If Eden starts with this item and immediately uses it in the starting room, the room will be reset, and all starting items and trinkets removed|r=Instead of the starting room being reset, Eden is taken to the starting room of {{S|Home}}. If used again in this room without having entered any other rooms, the room will be reset, and all starting items and trinkets removed except Glowing Hourglass}}.

