== Trivia ==
* In the book of Genesis, the Garden of Eden was the place where Adam and Eve lived before consuming the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, and thus being cast out by God.
** This technically makes Eden the only character in the game out of the main characters (excluding the secret characters of {{C|???}}, {{C|The Lost}}, {{C|Keeper}}, {{C|The Forgotten}} and their tainted variants) who is named after a biblical place rather than a person, since {{C|Bethany}}'s name can refer to both Mary of Bethany and the village of Bethany.
* According to Edmund, [https://archive.is/5CtVn Eden might not have a gender]. A quote from Edmund says “Eden is the fabled “mystery man” I’ve talked about in interviews before I had a fully realized idea of what they would become… see Eden isn’t a man, nor are they a woman.. they just are.“
* Eden could represent Isaac's rebirth as a new person, which explains why their stats and items are always random.
** Alternatively, Eden might represent Isaac's curiosity of experimenting with and discovering new things, which is common to virtually all children.
* Because of how Eden's stats work, Eden can start with a [[Luck]] stat containing values in lower decimal places.
** {{dlc|nr}} When actually used in most formulas, luck is rounded towards zero. This means Eden's effective starting luck is generally equivalent to 0.
** {{dlc|nr}} Playing as Eden is the only way to have non-integer luck. All other characters will always have a luck value of exactly a whole integer (e.g. 0.00, 1.00, etc.), as there are no items in the game that increase or decrease luck by any other value besides a whole integer.
* Eden's starting stats are listed as "?" on the character selection screen.
* Eden's locked character icon is [[Ending 1|the Locked Chest from ending 1]].
** Eden (and {{c|Tainted Eden}}) is the only character who can become locked again, returning to their locked character icon if the player runs out of tokens.
* During development, Edmund asked fans to contribute hairstyles for Eden. [https://twitter.com/EdmundMcMillenn/status/471133375437099009]
* On the release of ''The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth'', Eden had 5 hairstyles.
** {{dlc|a+}} 5 more were added in [[Booster_Packs#Booster Pack #1|Booster Pack #1]], and 25 more were added in [[Booster_Packs#Booster Pack #3|Booster Pack #3]] for ''[[Afterbirth+]]'', totalling 40 hairstyles.
** {{dlc|r+}} 14 more were added in ''[[Repentance+]]'', totalling 54 hairstyles.
* {{dlc|a+}} Some of Eden's hairstyles added in the Booster Packs resemble the hairstyles of other playable characters, being {{C|Azazel}}, {{C|Eve}}, {{C|Lazarus}}, {{C|Lilith}}, {{C|Magdalene}}, and {{C|Samson}}.
** {{dlc|r}} All of these hairstyles, except Azazel's, were changed in the [[V1.7.9b]] update to ''Repentance'' to reflect the updated hairstyles of each associated character.
** {{dlc|a+}} One of Eden's hairstyles references the [[Cut Content#Old Man Keeper|pre-release appearance]] of {{c|Keeper}}.
* {{dlc|a+}} Some of Eden's other hairstyles are pop-culture references to characters such as Elsa from ''Frozen'', Princess Leia from ''Star Wars'', Marzipan from ''Homestar Runner,'' Lucas from ''Mother 3'', and Frisk from ''Undertale.''

